      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "vulnerable_code_not_present",
      "impact_statement": "medh5 calls zlib only through compress2, uncompress, deflate and inflate on memory buffers (HDF5's deflate filter, C-Blosc2's zlib codec). Nothing it compiles in refers to the gzip file interface, so the linker never takes the gzwrite.c object from libz-sys's static archive: the 2.0.1 Linux wheels and an unstripped build of the 2.0.2 lock have no gz* symbol. SECURITY.md has the reasoning."
